---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const resumeHref = "/resume-michael-wyatt.pdf";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Michael Wyatt — Network Administrator at The Carter Center. 8+ years in network security, infrastructure, and cloud."
>
  <section class="pt-2 pb-6 flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">About</h1>
    <a
      href={resumeHref}
      download="Michael-Wyatt-Resume.pdf"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-border bg-muted px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-foreground hover:border-accent hover:text-accent transition-colors"
      aria-label="Download resume as PDF"
    >
      <svg
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        class="h-4 w-4"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4" />
        <polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10" />
        <line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3" />
      </svg>
      Download PDF
    </a>
  </section>

  <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
    <p class="lead">
      Experienced IT professional with 8+ years of expertise in network security, infrastructure
      deployment, and cloud management. Proven track record managing enterprise-grade Cisco
      environments, Azure cloud infrastructure, and SD-WAN implementations.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-fg">
      Hiram, GA 30141 · 678-901-7625 ·
      <a href="mailto:webdevmike01@gmail.com">webdevmike01@gmail.com</a><br />
      Willing to relocate: Chattanooga, TN · Atlanta, GA · Hiram, GA
    </p>
  </article>

  <hr class="my-10 border-border" />

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Work Experience</h2>

    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Network Administrator</h3>
          <span class="text-sm text-muted-fg">September 2023 – Present</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-fg">The Carter Center · Atlanta, GA</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Set up and managed multiple Cisco Firewalls across various locations using Firepower Management Center (FMC)</li>
          <li>Oversaw network infrastructure including servers, switches, and Azure cloud environments, ensuring efficiency and security</li>
          <li>Deployed and maintained high-availability VPN equipment for secure remote access via hairpinning</li>
          <li>Implemented SD-WAN solutions to improve network performance, reduce costs, and enhance reliability across multiple locations</li>
          <li>Led universal print rollout across the organization, streamlining printer management and reducing support overhead</li>
          <li>Developed scripts to automate routine network administration tasks, improving operational efficiency</li>
          <li>Led network upgrades ensuring minimal downtime and measurable performance enhancements</li>
          <li>Managed security policies, monitored network activity, and performed proactive threat mitigation</li>
          <li>Performed regular network audits to identify vulnerabilities and implemented necessary patches and updates</li>
          <li>Monitored network traffic using Wireshark to troubleshoot issues and ensure optimal performance</li>
          <li>Migrated legacy systems to modern networking technologies including SD-WAN and cloud-based solutions</li>
          <li>Configured VLANs, ACLs, and routing protocols (OSPF, BGP) to optimize network performance</li>
          <li>Implemented network monitoring stack via Docker (Prometheus, Grafana, Node Exporter) to proactively monitor server workloads and bandwidth anomalies</li>
          <li>Created detailed documentation of network configurations, troubleshooting procedures, and SOPs</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Desktop Administrator</h3>
          <span class="text-sm text-muted-fg">August 2018 – September 2023</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-fg">Vista Metals Georgia · Adairsville, GA</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Managed users, passwords, and permissions via Active Directory, Google Admin, and Office 365</li>
          <li>Installed and configured networking equipment including Cisco switches and Dell servers</li>
          <li>Supported desktops, copiers, tablets, phones, and industrial scale systems</li>
          <li>Gained expertise in VLAN, DHCP, TCP/IP, VPNs, and OS environments (Windows, Linux, RHEL, VMware)</li>
          <li>Diagnosed and resolved IT support tickets efficiently, ensuring seamless system performance</li>
          <li>Maintained network security through malware protection and Sophos antivirus solutions</li>
          <li>Resolved LAN/WAN connectivity issues and configured TCP/IP settings</li>
          <li>Provided remote support via RDP and VPN; guided end-users on backup and recovery best practices</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="my-10 border-border" />

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Education</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Bachelor of Science, Computer Information Systems</h3>
      <span class="text-sm text-muted-fg">September 2014 – May 2018</span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-fg">Shorter University · Rome, GA</p>
  </section>

  <hr class="my-10 border-border" />

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Skills</h2>

    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Networking</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Cisco Firewalls (FMC/FTD), SD-WAN, VPN (including hairpinned / high-availability), VLAN,
          ACL, OSPF, BGP, TCP/IP, DHCP, DNS, LAN/WAN, Meraki, Wireshark
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Cloud &amp; Infrastructure</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Azure Administration, Azure AD, Azure IaaS, ARM Templates, Azure Resource Manager, Cloud
          Networking, Load Balancing, Hyper-V, on-prem server rooms
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Security</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Network Security, Endpoint Security, Identity &amp; Access Management, Encryption, Log
          Analysis, Threat Mitigation, vulnerability audits
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Containers &amp; Orchestration</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Docker (multi-arch builds, read-only hardening, rootless), Kubernetes, Talos Linux,
          ArgoCD (GitOps), Longhorn, Prometheus, Grafana, Node Exporter, Helm
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">CI/CD Pipelines</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          GitHub Actions (matrix builds, OIDC, scoped PATs, image retention), multi-arch image
          publishing to GHCR and Docker Hub, semantic-version tag policies, lint-and-build gates
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Reverse Proxy &amp; Web</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          nginx (incl. nginx-unprivileged, read-only root filesystem hardening), Caddy, static-site
          delivery, Astro / Vue 3 frontends, TLS termination, header-based routing
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Agentic &amp; AI Infrastructure</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Built <a href="https://github.com/openlethe/lethe" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lethe</a>
          — a persistent memory layer for AI agents (Go + SQLite + SSE). OpenClaw plugin
          development, sub-agent orchestration, prompt and tool-design, deterministic and
          LLM-driven benchmark harnesses (HOTK-Bench, knowledge-transfer runs)
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Automation &amp; Scripting</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          PowerShell, Bash, Go, Vue 3 / TypeScript, REST and WebSocket APIs, cron / LaunchAgent
          scheduling, SOP-grade documentation
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Systems</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          Windows Server, RHEL, Ubuntu, Alpine, VMware, Virtualization, Active Directory, Office
          365, Google Workspace, Microsoft 365
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-fg mb-2">Other</h3>
        <p class="text-sm">
          SD-WAN, Universal Print, SQL, Leadership, Mentoring, Capacity Planning, SOP
          Documentation
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
